  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "In a physical balance working on the principle of moments, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>mg</mi></math> weight is placed on the left pan, the beam becomes horizontal. Both the empty pans of the balance are of equal mass. Which of the following statements is correct?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DfPbj",
      "text": "Every object that is weighed using this balance appears lighter than its actual weight",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kcdfX",
      "text": "Left arm is shorter than the right arm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "inaqN",
      "text": "Both the arms are of same length",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "m68bn",
      "text": "Left arm is longer than the right arm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>m</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>m</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> be the masses of pan<br /><br />It is given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/WhatsApp_Image_2020-05-19_at_3.12.18_AM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 174px;\" /><br /><br />Since&nbsp;balance is achieved, so net torque about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> should be zero.<br /><math> <mrow> <mfenced> <mrow> <mn>5</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><msub> <mi>m</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mi>g</mi></mrow> </mfenced><msub> <mi>r</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>=</mo><mfenced> <mrow> <msub> <mi>m</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mi>g</mi></mrow> </mfenced><msub> <mi>r</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So, left arm is shorter than the right arm.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
